Relevant columns and their potential usage  

• PYPI.PYPI.DISTRIBUTION_METADATA  
  – "name": package name (to match with downloads).  
  – "version": version string.  
  – "upload_time": pick the most‑recent release per package.  
  – "project_urls": VARIANT that may hold one or many URLs (flatten to extract).  
  – "home_page": fallback single URL when “project_urls” is NULL.  

• PYPI.PYPI.FILE_DOWNLOADS  
  – "project": package name (to aggregate download counts).  
  – "timestamp": can be used for optional period filters; not required here.  

Typical conditions / filters that will be useful  

1. Keep only rows where a GitHub URL exists:  
   •  (pu.value ILIKE '%github.com%')  OR ("home_page"  ILIKE '%github.com%')  

2. Keep the most‑recent version per package:  
   •  QUALIFY ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY "name" ORDER BY "upload_time" DESC)=1  

3. Clean the GitHub URL down to the core repo (no “issues”, “pull”, “blob”, “tree”, etc.):  
   •  REGEXP_REPLACE(url_text,
        '(/(issues|pull[^/]*|blob[^/]*|tree[^/]*))(/.*)*$' , '')  

Below are ten Snowflake SQL queries (LIMIT 20 for sampling) that progressively explore the data and culminate in the final step.  
All column names are wrapped in double quotes, and every query has a short comment header.

```sql
-- 1. Quick look at package names, versions, and upload times
SELECT DISTINCT 
       "name",
       "version",
       "upload_time"
FROM   "PYPI"."PYPI"."DISTRIBUTION_METADATA"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Inspect raw “project_urls” values for a handful of rows
SELECT 
       "name",
       "project_urls"
FROM   "PYPI"."PYPI"."DISTRIBUTION_METADATA"
WHERE  "project_urls" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Flatten “project_urls” to see individual keys / values
SELECT 
       dm."name",
       pu.key        AS "url_key",
       pu.value::STRING AS "url_val"
FROM   "PYPI"."PYPI"."DISTRIBUTION_METADATA"  dm,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => dm."project_urls") pu
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Sample GitHub‑oriented URLs coming from “project_urls”
SELECT DISTINCT 
       dm."name",
       pu.value::STRING AS "github_url"
FROM   "PYPI"."PYPI"."DISTRIBUTION_METADATA" dm,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => dm."project_urls") pu
WHERE  pu.value::STRING ILIKE '%github.com%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Same idea, but falling back to “home_page” when project_urls is missing
SELECT DISTINCT
       "name",
       "home_page" AS "github_url"
FROM   "PYPI"."PYPI"."DISTRIBUTION_METADATA"
WHERE  "home_page" ILIKE '%github.com%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Aggregate download counts by project (all time)
SELECT 
       "project",
       COUNT(*) AS "download_count"
FROM   "PYPI"."PYPI"."FILE_DOWNLOADS"
GROUP  BY "project"
ORDER  BY "download_count" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Determine the most recent distribution row per package
SELECT *
FROM   (
        SELECT *,
               ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY "name" ORDER BY "upload_time" DESC) AS rn
        FROM   "PYPI"."PYPI"."DISTRIBUTION_METADATA"
       )
WHERE  rn = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Combine latest metadata with any GitHub URL (project_urls first, else home_page)
SELECT 
       md."name",
       COALESCE(pu.value::STRING, md."home_page") AS "raw_github_url"
FROM   (
        SELECT *
        FROM   (
                SELECT *,
                       ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY "name" ORDER BY "upload_time" DESC) AS rn
                FROM   "PYPI"."PYPI"."DISTRIBUTION_METADATA"
               )
        WHERE  rn = 1
       ) md
       LEFT JOIN LATERAL FLATTEN(input => md."project_urls") pu
            ON TRUE
WHERE  COALESCE(pu.value::STRING, md."home_page") ILIKE '%github.com%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Same as #8 but with cleaned GitHub URLs (no issues/pull/blob/tree, lowercase for uniformity)
SELECT 
       LOWER(
           REGEXP_REPLACE(
               COALESCE(pu.value::STRING, md."home_page"),
               '(/(issues|pull[^/]*|blob[^/]*|tree[^/]*))(/.*)*$',
               ''
           )
       ) AS "clean_repo_url"
FROM   (
        SELECT *
        FROM   (
                SELECT *,
                       ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY "name" ORDER BY "upload_time" DESC) AS rn
                FROM   "PYPI"."PYPI"."DISTRIBUTION_METADATA"
               )
        WHERE  rn = 1
       ) md
       LEFT JOIN LATERAL FLATTEN(input => md."project_urls") pu
            ON TRUE
WHERE  COALESCE(pu.value::STRING, md."home_page") ILIKE '%github.com%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. FINAL: Top‑3 most downloaded packages that have valid GitHub repos (clean URLs only)
SELECT 
       TOP3."clean_repo_url"
FROM   (
        -- pull cleaned URL & tie to each package
        SELECT 
               LOWER(
                   REGEXP_REPLACE(
                       COALESCE(pu.value::STRING, md."home_page"),
                       '(/(issues|pull[^/]*|blob[^/]*|tree[^/]*))(/.*)*$',
                       ''
                   )
               )                          AS "clean_repo_url",
               md."name"
        FROM   (
                SELECT *
                FROM   (
                        SELECT *,
                               ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY "name" ORDER BY "upload_time" DESC) AS rn
                        FROM   "PYPI"."PYPI"."DISTRIBUTION_METADATA"
                       )
                WHERE  rn = 1
               ) md
               LEFT JOIN LATERAL FLATTEN(input => md."project_urls") pu
                    ON TRUE
        WHERE  COALESCE(pu.value::STRING, md."home_page") ILIKE '%github.com%'
        QUALIFY "clean_repo_url" IS NOT NULL
       ) GH
       JOIN (
             -- aggregate download counts
             SELECT 
                    "project",
                    COUNT(*) AS "download_count"
             FROM   "PYPI"."PYPI"."FILE_DOWNLOADS"
             GROUP  BY "project"
            ) DL
            ON GH."name" = DL."project"
       QUALIFY ROW_NUMBER() OVER (ORDER BY DL."download_count" DESC) <= 3
LIMIT 20;
```

